{
	title: 'EDIT operation headers accept trailing line comments',
	spec: 'The shared native-call parser extracts a trailing first-line // comment as a purpose, without changing quoted arguments, URLs, block comments or later lines. All tools accept it; tools with a description field use it when no explicit description or block-comment purpose was supplied. EDIT first-line headers accept it while literal old/new blocks remain untouched. EDIT cards honor a supplied description in call, success, unchanged and error titles; without one, filenames and change counts remain the title. Invariants restored: line comments can describe calls consistently, literal arguments remain data, and supplied EDIT descriptions stay visible.',
